---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import release from "../data/firmware.json";

const org = "https://github.com/ternmesh";
const notes = `${org}/firmware/releases/tag/v${release.version}`;
---

<Base
    title="Flash a board"
    description="Put Tern's firmware on a Heltec WiFi LoRa 32 V3 from your browser, over USB, with nothing to install."
>
    <section class="flash wrap">
        <h1>Put Tern on a board</h1>
        <p class="lede">
            This writes Tern {release.version} to a <strong>Heltec WiFi LoRa 32 V3</strong> over USB, from this page,
            with nothing to install. It takes about a minute.
        </p>
        <p id="unsupported" class="note" hidden>
            This browser cannot reach a USB serial port. Chrome and Edge on a computer can; Safari, Firefox and
            phones cannot yet. The <a href={notes}>release</a> has the images, to write another way.
        </p>

        <ul class="notes">
            <li>
                <strong>Fit the antenna first.</strong> The board sends by radio as soon as it starts, and sending
                with nothing on the antenna connector can damage it.
            </li>
            <li>
                It is for the Heltec V3 only (ESP32-S3 and SX1262, the 863-928 MHz kind). The page can tell that
                the chip is an ESP32-S3, not that the board is a Heltec: on another ESP32-S3 board the image
                is written and does not work.
            </li>
            <li>
                This is an alpha of a draft protocol. Its cryptography has not been reviewed: do not trust it
                with anything that matters. <a href={notes}>What it does and does not do.</a>
            </li>
        </ul>

        <form id="flash">
            <fieldset>
                <legend>Where will the board be used?</legend>
                <p class="muted">
                    It sends on this region's frequency from the moment it starts, so the wrong one breaks the
                    rules of the place you are in.
                </p>
                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="region" value="us915" required />
                    United States or Canada <span class="muted">US915: 921.25 MHz</span>
                </label>
                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="region" value="eu868" required />
                    Europe <span class="muted">EU868: 869.475 MHz, at most 10% of any hour</span>
                </label>
                <p class="muted">Anywhere else: there is no image yet. Do not use one of these.</p>
            </fieldset>

            <fieldset>
                <legend>What is on the board now?</legend>
                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="kind" value="new" required />
                    Something else, or nothing
                    <span class="muted">
                        replaces it, Meshtastic or MeshCore and their settings included; the board gets a new
                        Tern address
                    </span>
                </label>
                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="kind" value="update" required />
                    Tern already
                    <span class="muted">keeps its address, its sessions and its contacts</span>
                </label>
            </fieldset>

            <p>
                <button id="go" type="submit" class="primary">Flash over USB</button>
            </p>
            <p class="muted">
                The browser asks which port: the board's is usually the one named CP2102 or USB to UART. If
                the app or a terminal has the port open, close that first.
            </p>
        </form>

        <div id="working" class="card" hidden>
            <p id="status" role="status"></p>
            <progress id="bar"></progress>
            <p id="failed" class="muted" hidden>
                If the board would not go into its bootloader, hold its PRG button, press and let go of RST, let
                go of PRG, and try again. A cable that only charges does this too.
            </p>
            <p id="done" hidden>
                <a class="button" href="/app">Open the app</a>
            </p>
            <details>
                <summary>What the flasher said</summary>
                <pre id="log"></pre>
            </details>
        </div>

        <p class="muted small">
            The images are the <a href={notes}>v{release.version} release</a>'s, checked here against its{" "}
            <a href="/firmware/SHA256SUMS">SHA-256 checksums</a> before a byte is written, and written with
            Espressif's <a href="https://github.com/espressif/esptool-js">esptool-js</a>.
        </p>
    </section>
</Base>

<script>
    import "../lib/flash/page.ts";
</script>

<style>
    .flash {
        padding-top: 32px;
        padding-bottom: 48px;
        max-width: 48rem;
    }
    [hidden] {
        display: none !important;
    }
    h1 {
        font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.6rem);
        margin: 0 0 12px;
    }
    .lede {
        font-size: 1.1rem;
    }
    .notes {
        padding-left: 1.2em;
    }
    .notes li {
        margin-bottom: 6px;
    }
    .note,
    .card {
        background: var(--accent-soft);
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: var(--radius);
        padding: 10px 14px;
    }
    .card {
        background: var(--surface);
        margin: 16px 0;
    }
    fieldset {
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: var(--radius);
        margin: 16px 0;
        padding: 10px 14px;
    }
    legend {
        font-weight: 600;
        padding: 0 6px;
    }
    fieldset label {
        display: block;
        padding: 6px 0;
        cursor: pointer;
    }
    fieldset label .muted {
        display: block;
        margin-left: 1.6em;
        font-size: 0.9rem;
    }
    fieldset p {
        margin: 4px 0;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
    }
    button,
    a.button {
        display: inline-block;
        font: inherit;
        padding: 9px 16px;
        border-radius: var(--radius);
        border: 1px solid var(--accent);
        background: var(--accent);
        color: var(--bg);
        font-weight: 600;
        cursor: pointer;
        text-decoration: none;
    }
    button:disabled {
        opacity: 0.5;
        cursor: not-allowed;
    }
    progress {
        width: 100%;
        height: 12px;
        accent-color: var(--accent);
    }
    #status.bad {
        color: #b3261e;
    }
    @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        #status.bad {
            color: #f2b8b5;
        }
    }
    pre {
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        max-height: 16rem;
        overflow: auto;
        white-space: pre-wrap;
    }
    .small {
        font-size: 0.9rem;
    }
</style>
